id: pm-todos-cross-file
title: Coordinate row ownership across selected TODO files
description: "Acceptance: moving one identified row between two selected files updates ownership once; duplicate source ownership refuses; a stale second file prevents an atomic selection from applying; unrelated files stay outside scope. Reuse the reviewed todo.txt session planner and core SDK transactions. Include typed SDK and CLI contracts, bounded TOON/JSON receipts, strict input schema, revision-bound recovery, seeded model tests, read-only public-data validation and packed installation coverage."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-todos#162"
created_at: "2026-10-27T17:28:50.173Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T19:06:32.446Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Moving one identified row between two selected files updates ownership once; duplicate source ownership refuses; a stale second file prevents an atomic selection from applying; unrelated files remain outside scope
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T17:29:45.992Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core public workspace transactions and immutable item history already provide coordination and recovery; pm-todos glob import collects files and sessions reconcile one exchange; pm-csv roundtrip coordinates spreadsheet rows, and pm-memory owns memory projections. No existing cross-file TODO ownership selection was found. Reuse the todo.txt session planner, native SDK reads, mutations, locks and workspace transactions; no new import engine. The pinned SDK is 2026.10.23, retained per dependency policy; public registry currently reports 2026.10.27."
  "2026-10-27T17:45:03.000Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: explicit source manifest and per-row immutable history revisions; reuse fidelity/session normalization and the same planner for preview, apply and recovery. Public SDK owns fenced selection leases, native item locks, append-only item histories and workspace transaction journals. No additional import engine. Added CLI export/preview/apply and individually skipped export refusals. Read-only public validation at main 847bc287: 102 rows inspected, 101 selected, 1 unsupported row skipped, 2 files, 11413 text bytes and 106696 manifest bytes; duplicate ownership refused and complete copied-file fingerprint unchanged. Native race compensation retains peer success and reports superseded instead of overwriting an already touched row."
  "2026-10-27T17:55:23.388Z",codex-agent,"Packed compatibility testing found that the declared 2026.10.20 minimum lacks the public acquireLockLease declaration in both sdk/runtime.d.ts and core/lock/lock.d.ts. Raise only the supported peer/manifest minimum to the existing development pin 2026.10.23; the development dependency is unchanged. npm-global and bun-global packed moves/read-back/replays already pass. The seeded model also exposed unsafe native history round-trips for an own __proto__ metadata key; new source inputs refuse that key before writes, with an explicit remedy. Ordinary prototype-named keys are checked with own-property semantics."
  "2026-10-27T17:59:08.653Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy only, removing assertRevision made the duplicate-ownership/stale-second-file regression fail (exit 1): the stale second row was accepted and the expected refusal disappeared. The package worktree was never altered for the revert; the fixed regression is rerun with the targeted tests. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to CI per the shared-host resource rule."
  "2026-10-27T18:15:09.631Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test execution passed all 41 targeted tests, including 500 seeded operation sequences across ten real non-git trackers (zero failed, canceled or skipped). The test runner used its default schema context; result tracking is disabled, so this comment preserves the measured receipt rather than changing project policy. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint passed (19 files, 125 declarations). Follow-up pm-todos-native-kv-codec records the native prototype-key history limitation. Post-review hardening refuses non-JSON object/array shapes and retains partial export files so cleanup cannot delete a peer edit; focused schema/CLI regressions cover those changes. Initial CI is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/40556712342; full npm and Bun gates are not yet evidence."
  "2026-10-27T18:20:10.353Z",codex-agent,"Final local acceptance: updated schema/CLI regressions passed 2/2; moving-row/duplicate regressions passed 2/2, including a bound-row move with changed=applied=moved=1, exactly one appended native event and byte-identical history for the other selected row. Packed npm-global and bun-global probes both passed on pm CLI 2026.10.26, two source rows each and replay changed=0, using identical artifact SHA256 c75b49cd84c75e316213d798854cb065e422587871ff45c8337cefc4b5908c9d. The initial CI jobs remain queued for hosted runners; 0 of 4 npm/Bun release-gate executions have completed. Keep this item open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T18:25:02.401Z",codex-agent,"Initial Node 26 CI executed 384 tests: 383 passed, with the sole failure an existing installed-package assertion expecting six extension fields after this feature adds the seventh todos_source_file field. Coverage still exceeded unchanged thresholds: 99.03 percent lines, 93.21 percent branches, 99.65 percent functions. Updated the registration-count contract and reran the rich JSONL integration plus schema fuzz tests. Local strict health is clean after installing the exact project pm-github version already used in CI; the earlier local host-version skew came from the ambient global extension, not the project package."
  "2026-10-27T18:26:29.868Z",codex-agent,"The CI-discovered registration-count fix is verified: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"schema fuzz|installed package preserves\" test/source-sessions.test.ts test/integration.test.ts passed 2/2, including the real packed rich-JSONL import/export/sync path. Current local strict health is ok with zero findings. Initial CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/40556712342 has one failed npm gate (the fixed count assertion), one skipped Bun gate and the second Node matrix job still queued. A fresh exact-head CI run is required after this final push."
  "2026-10-27T18:31:08.595Z",codex-agent,"Added the interleaving between a second row preparation and its native write: a foreign skipped step cannot decrement the retained-write count for another row. Compensation/interleaving tests pass 2/2; reverting only that count guard in a disposable copy fails 0 versus 1, and the unchanged fixed checkout passes again 1/1. Partial export failures retain files instead of deleting possible peer edits. All tracker writes are complete; full exact-head CI remains required after the final push. The claim was released and both items remain open."
  "2026-10-27T18:35:08.513Z",codex-agent,"CI handoff receipt for runtime commit 7024bb6: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/40560848071 remains queued for both Node 22.18.0 and Node 26; zero of four full npm/Bun release gates have passed. The original 30-minute CI cutoff is retained and is not reset by this evidence-only commit. The initial 383/384 CI assertion failure was fixed and its integration test passed locally; canceled superseded checks are not approval. Final-head release evidence remains pending for orchestrator verification. No merge or release was performed."
  "2026-10-28T15:37:14.757Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 resumed after a clean worktree check and merge of origin/main. General rule: recovery must recognize every transaction-owned durable phase, including append-only compensation, before revision guards can reject a plan; a peer revision must still refuse. Package-wide search covers sessions, recurrence, watcher, CLI transport, JSON/TOON and packed acceptance. The supplied report contains one blocker and GitHub has no actionable inline findings. Previous head CI eventually passed both Node matrices; fresh gates are required for this fix."
  "2026-10-28T16:05:45.821Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: only source-sessions owns a compensating workspace transaction. Every source SDK/CLI entry now shares a three-state native-history classifier at preflight, inspection, preparation, locked apply and compensation. It proves the baseline prefix, alternating owned phases, preservation of unowned state and exact compensation values through public SDK replay/canonicalization. Single-file sessions, recurrence and watcher have no rollback journal and need no equivalent phase change. All 21 new no-git/no-git-on-PATH tests passed, covering every rollback boundary with two/three rows, custom statuses, host injection, repeated interruptions, peer revisions and copied markers. Two isolated behavioral reverts each fail: forward-only recovery returns stale_revision; trusting compensation markers without lineage accepts a peer revision. Fixed checkout rerun passes 2/2. No additional actionable findings were supplied or found in GitHub review threads."
  "2026-10-28T16:14:26.288Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test execution also passed the recovery matrix 21/21 with zero failures/skips. Packed focus passed both npm minimum host 2026.10.23 in JSON and Bun global host 2026.10.26 in TOON, each recovering an interrupted two-row rollback through the installed artifact and real consumer CLI; artifact SHA256 7b2cbafb5f8635ab884b01c7fb824585596eb32f5a82ffa55c61da3d0e374df6 was identical. Strict health has zero findings. Starting the full npm and Bun release gates serially; coverage runner is explicitly capped at two workers, thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-28T16:48:27.496Z",codex-agent,"Validation update: the revised packed driver passes npm-minimum on host 2026.10.23, resolving the supported SDK from its installed consumer context. The artifact remains sha256 7b2cbafb5f8635ab884b01c7fb824585596eb32f5a82ffa55c61da3d0e374df6. All 21 recovery tests also passed under coverage in the full npm attempt. That local attempt hit the existing recurrence model test timeout at 600 seconds after 100 sequences (166 imports, 245 exports, 79 syncs, 137 older replays, 126 CRLF variants); no assertion failed before the timeout. Stopped that failed process tree, including the unfinished source model test, to avoid wasting the saturated host. No timeouts, assertions, sequence counts or coverage thresholds were weakened. Following the original host constraint, the npm and Bun CI release gates are the full-suite evidence; local full gates are not claimed green. Strict tracker health has zero findings."
  "2026-10-28T16:52:17.456Z",codex-agent,"The final package-wide audit finds one compensating coordinator in source-sessions.ts, reached by standalone SDK and injected CLI paths; sessions, recurrence and watchers do not own another rollback journal. Every revision guard now uses the same baseline/applied/compensated classifier. The revised installed-consumer driver passes npm minimum-host recovery. Its first Bun-global run exposed a harness assumption about the global package directory; supported BUN_INSTALL_GLOBAL_DIR and BUN_INSTALL_BIN now explicitly bind both destinations to the isolated fixture. The installed-artifact recovery assertion is the regression for that harness class; rerun pending. No actionable non-blocking review comments were supplied or present in the PR inline comments."
  "2026-10-28T17:04:34.142Z",codex-agent,"Final focused validation: the host-managed installed-artifact driver passes node scripts/accept-packed.ts npm-minimum (SDK 2026.10.23, JSON) and node scripts/accept-packed.ts bun-global (SDK 2026.10.26, TOON). Each receipt reports 2 source rows, replay changed 0, rollback_recovered true and identical artifact sha256 7b2cbafb5f8635ab884b01c7fb824585596eb32f5a82ffa55c61da3d0e374df6. The driver uses the installed extension public entry and SDK loader, independent of npm/Bun storage layout; Bun receives explicit isolated global destinations/config. This corrects the earlier harness directory assumption; both final runs pass. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (21 files/129 declarations), changelog generation/check and strict health pass. All 21 recovery adversarial cases pass through the linked pm runner, and both behavioral revert proofs are recorded above. The supplied blocker is fixed across every native revision guard; no additional actionable inline findings exist. Full npm/Bun release gates will run in final-commit CI with two workers and unchanged thresholds. Local timeout evidence is retained above, not represented as a passing gate. Claim released for orchestrator review; items stay unclosed."
  "2026-10-28T17:50:04.756Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 blocker confirmed. General rule: a transaction marker is correlation, not proof of intended state; every claimed forward event must equal the producer-derived target on all owned fields, including fields the edit leaves unchanged, and every compensation must match the native baseline. Round 1 proved preserved fields and restored compensation but omitted forward-value equality. Rechecked clean worktree and tracker; origin/main is already an ancestor, so no merge is needed. Package audit again finds one compensating coordinator shared by SDK and CLI; no additional actionable inline findings or review-body findings were supplied. Plan: reconstruct immutable baseline documents from SDK-verified history, derive intended values with the same planner and patch application as real writes, validate each native event against that intent at every guard, add field-complete copied-marker/hidden-intermediate-event tests and packed JSON/TOON refusals, and preserve all existing recovery tests and thresholds."
  "2026-10-28T18:11:54.169Z",codex-agent,"Focused native recovery suite passed through the linked pm runner: 43 tests, 43 passes, zero failures/skips/cancellations, in 511.7 seconds within its existing 600-second linked-test limit. Coverage includes all nine producer-owned fields in edit and move-only selections, forged forward events hidden by subsequent compensation, corrupt compensation data, a real SDK coordinator completing only a subset, and every previous valid rollback case. Results are recorded here because project test-result tracking is disabled; policy was not changed. The expected projection is verification intent only: actual writes still re-read all selected revisions and call the same planner under native mutation locks. Added a separate explicit two-row copied-owner regression as well; its focused run is next. No test assertion, native timeout or coverage threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-28T18:15:34.714Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert audit caught a fixture error before commit: the new three-row field corpus chose its poison target by creation order, while the coordinator uses manifest source order. Those cases were rejecting repeated apply events on an already-applied row, so the earlier 43-pass result does not prove the missing forward-value check. Corrected the target to the last manifest step and added an assertion that its actual last native event is compensation. Hidden-intermediate-event restoration now uses that exact row baseline too. Rerunning the corrected corpus and isolated behavioral reverts; no passing evidence is claimed for the old target choice. The packed minimum SDK 2026.10.23 check independently passed the actual two-row recovery and JSON copied-marker refusal, including SDK-canonical document/body/history equality after both preview and apply."
  "2026-10-28T18:28:13.052Z",codex-agent,"Corrected final native suite: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/source-recovery.test.ts passed all 44 tests through the pm runner, zero failures/skips/cancellations. It asserts the poisoned target actually ended in compensation before each attack. Behavioral revert proofs in disposable copies: removing only the forward intended-value comparison from revisionState fails 3 tests (exact two-row copied-owner case, three-row ownership case, hidden poisoned priority event); reverting only the compensation-data validation/restoration block fails the native history preservation test; removing only the final selection completeness check fails the real-SDK subset-coordinator test. Restoring the fixed implementation passes all 5 controls, with no changes to the package worktree during mutation checks. No assertions, native test timeouts or coverage thresholds changed. Broader package audit: editing sessions replan against locked native values; recurrence storedReceipt compares fresh stored scheduling facts with requested intent before created/rescheduled success; import/sync writes use SDK updates; the watcher only queues revision-bound proposals. Those paths do not accept a copied marker as completion of a cross-file selection. All source-session guard paths share the corrected classifier and final native read-back check."
  "2026-10-28T19:06:30.623Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 focused evidence: corrected native recovery corpus 44/44 passed through the pm runner; the 3 additional pending-row lease-boundary cases also passed through pm, covering prepared, step_applied and step_recorded with foreign values/history preserved and package-only compensation. Removing only the intended-value comparison fails all 3 pending-boundary tests; restoring it passes all 3 controls. Together with the earlier 3 rollback-forward failures, compensation-data failure and incomplete-coordinator failure, 4 disposable mutation runs fail 8 regressions and restored controls pass 8/8. All 47 distinct recovery cases pass. A malformed linked command was corrected using --add-json after --add treated JSON as a literal command; no test had executed from that entry, and all audit history is retained. Final packed npm minimum 2026.10.23 JSON and Bun global 2026.10.26 TOON checks pass recovery plus copied-marker refusal in preview/apply, with full SDK-canonical document/body/history equality afterward. Artifact sha256 540ad070a6e0983ab7a8a802f0d3bb0979e6d51fdd77a155c1a2198371528e5a. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass (21 files, 132 declarations). The local full npm attempt at two workers again hit the existing 600-second recurrence model timeout after 100 sequences (166 imports, 245 exports, 79 syncs, 137 older replays, 126 CRLF variants); stopped its process tree and unfinished source model. No full local gate is claimed green, and no assertion, timeout, sequence count or threshold changed. Following the original saturated-host constraint, final npm/Bun full-gate evidence will come from CI at two workers. All supplied actionable findings are fixed; no additional actionable review comments exist. Release claim for orchestrator review; keep items unclosed."
